The Mercedes-Benz A160 CDI was part of the W176 generation (2012-2018). Based on the search results, the A160 CDI (also referred to as A160d after the 2015 facelift) typically had a 1.5L diesel engine producing 90 hp and 240 Nm (177 lb-ft) of torque. It was available with a manual or automatic transmission. 0-60 mph acceleration is estimated around 12.1 to 13.1 seconds, and top speed is around 112 mph (180 km/h). Fuel economy is quite good, with combined figures around 64-76 UK mpg (58.8-61.9 US mpg). CO2 emissions are low, around 98-105 g/km. The car's dimensions are around 4292-4299 mm length, 1780 mm width, and 1433 mm height, with a wheelbase of 2699 mm. Cargo space is around 341-1157 L (12-40.9 cu ft). Turning circle is around 11m (36.09 ft). The W176 A-Class received a 5-star Euro NCAP safety rating. Insurance groups for the W176 A-Class range from 13 to 33, with the A160 CDI likely being on the lower end. Used prices for 2014-2015 A160 CDI models are typically in the £7,800 - £12,990 range. Reliability is generally considered good for the diesel engine, though some sources mention potential issues with the fuel injection system and timing belt, as well as potential issues with the DCT transmission if equipped. Interior quality is noted as being very Mercedes-Benz, though some lower plastics can be brittle and lead to squeaks.

